7;ll learn how to ask S-Lady to find a family member through Find My so you don&#8217;t have to call them, and why Command-Backtick (one key up from Tab) cycles windows inside a single app while Command-1, 2, 3 hops tabs in Safari, Chrome, Comet, and even Mail. You&#8217;ll follow Dave down the iPhone system data rabbit hole, where 59GB of mystery storage led to a full wipe, a genuinely useful &#8220;keep eSIMs and erase data&#8221; option, and then 52GB creeping right back three days later. You&#8217;ll turn an always-on Mac mini into an AirPlay music server you drive from the Remote app, so the party keeps playing after you make a beer run. You&#8217;ll discover that Terminal&#8217;s Secure Keyboard Entry checkbox is why your TextExpander and Rocket Typist snippets quit firing. And you&#8217;ll hear the cheapest Wi-Fi fix in history: delete the speed test app. Plus, AI as a genealogy research partner: the kind that surfaces buried leads you verify yourself.</p>
